// %open and %edit typed in the REPL (plan §7f, the IDE layer): `madc -i`
// loads this file, then the entries in testrepl_opencmd.input run. The
// terminal's editor is $EDITOR (testrepl_opencmd.env sets echo, which prints
// what it was given): %open FILE gives it FILE, which need not exist, and
// %edit NAME gives it `+LINE` and the file a session unit defined NAME in —
// this file's `base` at its line, a loaded file's function at its own.

